This product contains original software developed for the ED-209 and R2-D2
operator-guard projects. It bundles no third-party source code. The runtime
uses only the Python standard library; pytest is a test-only dependency and is
not bundled.

Provenance caveats:

- The rulepacks are `documented-initial` plus documented protected-path
  additions. They are NOT the absent 161-rule legacy ED-209 export and must not
  be presented as full parity.
- `src/operator_guards/ed209/source_policy.py` is a port of the live ED-209
  provenance module. It is an optional, separate layer and is not wired into the
  Hermes plugin's runtime rule loader.
- The Linux observer supports a closed, documented predicate set.
  `takeover_without_send` is unsupported and is reported as such.
- Same-UID processes are not security-isolated from one another. These guards
  are procedural defence-in-depth, not an OS security boundary.
